      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-159689",
      ":question/problem": "Let $X = [X_{1}, X_{2}]^{T}$ be a bivariate normal random vector. The variances of $X_{1}$ and $X_{2}$ and their covariance are given by\n\n$\u03c3_{1}^{2} = 10, \u03c3_{2}^{2} = 5, \u03c3_{12} = 5$.\n\nGiven that the joint probability density function of $X$ is\n$f(x) = \\frac{1}{k}\\exp(-\\frac{1}{2}(x - \u03bc)^{T}\u03a3^{-1}(x - \u03bc))$,\n\nwhere $\u03bc$ is the mean vector and $\u03a3$ is the corresponding covariance matrix, find the value of $k$."
